{{#if (listeningApps)}}
{{#if (isMono)}}
An app that listens on a port takes it from the `PORT` environment variable: the commands above run one app on another port from its directory. `PORT` on the root `{{runScript "dev"}}` reaches every app, which then all listen on that port.
{{else}}
The app listens on port {{appPort appName}}. Set `PORT` to listen on another one: `PORT=4000 {{runScript "dev"}}`.
{{/if}}
{{#if (hasRootScript "start")}}
`start` takes `PORT` the same way.
{{/if}}
{{#if (appOriginEnvs)}}
{{#if (or (hasAppScript "start") (hasAppScript "preview"))}}

The variables below hold the origin each app is served from. The authentication check of a production server compares the origin of a request with it (a request from another origin is refused), and the server calls its own app through it. After changing the port, set them to the new origin (`http://localhost:4000`) in the `.env` of the app and build again, with the build command of the production steps, before `start` or `preview`: the values a framework exposes to the browser are frozen at build.

